  "id": "COMPOUND:43491 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Methyl valerate is implicated in the interaction with A2780cisR through a series of molecular pathways, with Caspase-5 acting as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that Methyl valerate targets Caspase-5, which in turn targets A2780cisR via different metabolic intermediates, including 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid and Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, as well as Diplotrin A. These pathways highlight a complex network of interactions, where Methyl valerate exerts its effects through multiple distinct chemical entities that ultimately converge on A2780cisR. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Caspase-5 as a critical node in the signaling cascade, with Methyl valerate potentially modulating the activity of this enzyme to influence the expression of A2780cisR. The evidence supports a mechanism where Methyl valerate's effects are mediated through Caspase-5, which in turn modulates A2780cisR via various biochemical intermediates, suggesting a broader role in cellular signaling and regulation.",
